doctype html

- var title = "Assorted thoughts on IDE features, that must've been available for 10 years now"

head
	title #{title}
	<link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="general.css">
	<script id="MathJax-script" async src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@4/tex-mml-chtml.js"></script>
body
	div
		h1 #{title}
		h2 CRDT-based document history
		p 
			| Because Git sucks. 
			| Will allow late commits (commiting the past) and live collaborative editing of the code.
			| No edit will be lost.
			| A major topic that is a food for thought by itself.
		h2 Painting over document
		p 
			| Just give the user brush, colors and eraser. Anchor drawings to the nearest line of code. 
			| Version control them.
			| Will significantly assist in developing and debugging algorithms.
		h2 Graphical debugging and oscillocsopes
		ul
			li Indispensable in audio DSP work.
			li An IDE may work like a Unity/Godot editor and provide own framebuffer to application for ease of prototyping.
			li 
				a(href="https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=AdamWulkiewicz.GraphicalDebugging") For Visual Studio.
			li 
				| Oscilloscopes are external libraries that communicate with an IDE to provide inline oscilloscope of 
				| recorded in the current debug session values. 
				| An oscilloscope may be a function taking any value. 
				| An IDE may provide a way to filter and display a graph with value of the specific field in given structs.
		h2 Code bubbles
		ul
			li To make more efficient use of screen space.
			li
				a(href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PsPX0nElJ0k") Original Code Bubbles editor
			li 
				a(href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c2uZnR5D_cc") Haystack editor — code bubbles for VSCode (ded((( )
		h2 Programmable search and replace
		ul
			li Commands of vi/vim.
			li Structural regexps of sam/acme.
			li Syntax-aware rewrite by example.
		h2 Elastic tabstops
		ul
			li To unify text and tables so all text-based features can be used on table data.
			li 
				a(href="https://nick-gravgaard.com/elastic-tabstops/") Original proposing blog article.
			li
				a(href="https://github.com/nick-gravgaard/AlwaysAlignedVS") Again, Visual Studio exclusive extension.
		h2 Trivial extensibility
		p 
			| A plugin in its simplest form must be a file in the specified directory of other plugins like it.
			| An IDE must
			b  know
			|  and
			b  suggest
			|  its API to the plugin developer.

		h2 Points of interest
		ul
			li 
				a(href="https://github.com/lite-xl/lite-xl") Lite-XL, a good candidate for implementing these ideas
			li 
				a(href="https://www.inkandswitch.com/patchwork") Ink&Switch's Patchwork
			li 
				a(href="https://www.flinto.com/") Flinto
			li 
				a(href="https://github.com/tonsky/Clojure-Sublimed") Clojure Sublimed